rguing with their mother about which clothes they could have; or Nuremberg women wearing false braids dyed red or green. This brilliantly illustrated book draws on a range of insights across the disciplines and allows us to see an entire period in new ways. In integrating its findings into larger arguments about consumption, visual culture, the Reformation, German history, and the relationship of European and global history, it promises to re-shape the field.","pageCount":354,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"History","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-dressing-up-cultural-identity-in-renaissance-europe-ulinka-rublack"}],"displaySummary":"This brilliantly illustrated book draws on a range of insights across the disciplines and allows us to see an entire period in new ways. In integrating its findings into larger arguments about consumption, visual culture, the Reformation, German history, and the relationship of European and global history, it promises to re-shape the field.","primaryTopic":"Europe & Russia","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"History","confidence":"high","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"History","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"History","mappedSubject":"History","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily explores historical themes through the lens of cultural identity and visual representation in Renaissance Europe, making 'History' the dominant subject along with a significant focus on 'Society & Culture'.","id":"subject-evidence-book-dressing-up-cultural-identity-in-renaissance-europe-ulinka-rublack-1"},{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","rawLabel":"History","mappedSubject":"History","score":3,"confidence":"medium","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-dressing-up-cultural-identity-in-renaissance-europe-ulinka-rublack","id":"subject-evidence-book-dressing-up-cultural-identity-in-rena